vnStat: graphs drawn in the page from vnstat's JSON, instead of vnstati pictures

Status -> Traffic Monitor -> Graphs showed every chart as a PNG that vnstati drew on the
router: a white box in its own grey and green, whatever the theme or dark mode, fixed in size,
its text not selectable, its values readable only by eye. vnstati also brings libgd, libpng and
libwebp into the image, and nothing else uses them.

The page now reads `vnstat --json a -i <interface>` (one call per interface, every 60 seconds
as before) and draws everything itself:

- Summary: tiles for today, yesterday, this month (with the month's estimate at the rate so
  far), last month and all time, each split into RX and TX, and the last 24 hours as a chart.
- Top: the busiest days as a table, with the average rate and a bar for each day's share.
- 5 Minute (last 6 hours), Hourly (last 48 hours), Daily (last 30 days), Monthly (last 12
  months), Yearly (every year on record): a stacked RX/TX bar chart. Hovering or tapping a
  bar shows its time, RX, TX, total and average rate; the newest slot's rate is over the time
  so far. Each chart has its numbers as a table under "Show as a table".

Slots with no traffic, which vnstat keeps no entry for, show as zero rather than closing up,
and nothing is drawn for the time before the interface was added. Times are the router's own,
as vnstat reports them. The colours come from the theme's chart tokens (--v-chart-1 for RX,
--v-chart-2 for TX) and the borders and text from the Bootstrap tokens every theme in the image
publishes, with plain fallbacks for any other theme.

The ACL swaps the vnstati command for that one vnstat command, the menu entry no longer asks
for /usr/bin/vnstati, and the package no longer depends on vnstati2, so the image drops it and
its image libraries. "Clear data for all interfaces" works as before.

Applies to: the luci feed pin, applications/luci-app-vnstat2.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

